  "worked_solution": "Since $g(x)$ is left-continuous at $x=5,$ we have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {5}^{-}}g(x)=g(5)=5.\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {5}^{-}}\\frac{g(x)-{x}^{2}}{4x} & =\\frac{{lim}_{x\\to {5}^{-}}g(x)-\\text{\u00a0}{lim}_{x\\to {5}^{-}}{x}^{2}}{{lim}_{x\\to {5}^{-}}4x} \\\\  & =\\frac{5-{5}^{2}}{4(5)} \\\\  & =\\frac{5-25}{20} \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
